{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7488b089-0b74-4beb-bb18-b47868c84310","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f4e6ee85d5d255a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-aibnttob/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md","content":"# FIPS 140-3 conversion of KServe serving-stack images\n\n## Description\n\nConverts the KServe serving-stack images so they run correctly on FIPS-enabled\nOpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated\ncrypto in the request path. The epic covers the audit of current cryptographic\nlibrary linkage, the conversion to validated modules, verification on a\nFIPS-enabled cluster, and the CI regression enforcement covering KServe image\nbuilds.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all KServe serving-stack images to inventory every linked cryptographic\n  library and its validation status; the audit determines the exact set of\n  images needing conversion (the strategy says \"several images\" without\n  enumerating them).\n- Replace non-validated cryptographic library usage with validated modules\n  throughout the request path.\n- Rebuild the converted images and verify correct serving operation on a\n  FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster.\n- Author and verify the CI gating check covering KServe image builds that\n  fails any build reintroducing non-validated crypto usage — the KServe-surface\n  portion of the FIPS regression enforcement, owned here because it enforces\n  over exactly the images this epic converts.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A cryptographic module inventory exists for every KServe serving-stack image,\n  listing each linked crypto library and its validation status.\n- All KServe serving-stack images run correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift\n  cluster using validated crypto modules, with no non-validated crypto in the\n  request path, verified by test.\n- The CI gating check covering KServe image builds fails a build that\n  reintroduces non-validated crypto usage, verified by a test that intentionally\n  reintroduces such usage and observes the gate fail.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0) — KServe-image portion: images run on FIPS-enabled clusters with\n  validated crypto, no non-validated crypto in the request path.\n- HLR-3 (P1) — KServe-surface portion of the CI FIPS regression check\n  (bundled: the check enforces over the same images this epic converts, so it\n  is not separately schedulable).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The strategy does not enumerate which images link non-validated crypto; the\n  scope audit resolves this and does not change the epic's shape.\n- \"Serving data plane\" is interpreted as the KServe predictor data plane. If\n  model-serving runtime images are also in scope, that work belongs to a\n  separate strategy and epic set.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47154,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-985c5dfd08bf1e09","agent_id":"a78871ae114a39812","session_id":"44bb4be5-e725-48c0-870c-d3c41c68193e","uuid":"232ee514-fb3b-4619-bb55-65012af818b8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:10:01.401Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
