s non-validated crypto usage, verified by a test that\n  intentionally reintroduces such usage and observes the gate fail.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0) — Platform Operator portion: operator images run on FIPS-enabled\n  clusters with validated crypto.\n- HLR-3 (P1) — operator-surface portion of the CI FIPS regression check\n  (bundled: the check enforces over the same images this epic converts, so it\n  is not separately schedulable).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- No architecture-context file is provisioned for the Platform Operator, so its\n  repo and image layout are unverified; confirm at implementation start. The\n  component is treated as existing (it is in the canonical RHAI component list\n  and the strategy presumes its images already ship).\n- The owning team is inferred (the strategy has no team table) and should be\n  confirmed by a human.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47154,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-985c5dfd08bf1e09","agent_id":"a78871ae114a39812","session_id":"44bb4be5-e725-48c0-870c-d3c41c68193e","uuid":"b6d556b4-2a4c-4818-9e6c-c5f890cb0e0a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:10:06.836Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
