 FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules with no\n  non-validated crypto in the request path.\n- The evidence package is submitted through the security review board to the\n  external certification laboratory, and the submission is triaged/acknowledged\n  by the laboratory.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0) — full: compliance evidence package (module inventory, build\n  attestations, test results) assembled and submitted through the security\n  review board to the external certification lab.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Laboratory turnaround is historically six to nine months and security review\n  board sign-off occurs at defined milestones; both are externally controlled\n  and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. This epic's deliverable ends\n  at submission and triage — the certification outcome and its timing are\n  outside the strategy's control.\n- The package spans the whole serving stack (KServe components and the\n  Platform Operator); the KServe component is recorded as the primary Jira\n  component for routing.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47154,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-985c5dfd08bf1e09","agent_id":"a78871ae114a39812","session_id":"44bb4be5-e725-48c0-870c-d3c41c68193e","uuid":"a9c8d299-70f8-4bce-bb73-912d5f2e93d5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:10:13.099Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
