{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6dddcd0188c4d05","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 conversion of KServe serving-stack images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS 140-3 conversion of KServe serving-stack images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tConverts the KServe serving-stack images so they run correctly on FIPS-enabled\n34\tOpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated\n35\tcrypto in the request path. The epic covers the audit of current cryptographic\n36\tlibrary linkage, the conversion to validated modules, verification on a\n37\tFIPS-enabled cluster, and the CI regression enforcement covering KServe image\n38\tbuilds.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Audit all KServe serving-stack images to inventory every linked cryptographic\n43\t  library and its validation status; the audit determines the exact set of\n44\t  images needing conversion (the strategy says \"several images\" without\n45\t  enumerating them).\n46\t- Replace non-validated cryptographic library usage with validated modules\n47\t  throughout the request path.\n48\t- Rebuild the converted images and verify correct serving operation on a\n49\t  FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster.\n50\t- Author and verify the CI gating check covering KServe image builds that\n51\t  fails any build reintroducing non-validated crypto usage — the KServe-surface\n52\t  portion of the FIPS regression enforcement, owned here because it enforces\n53\t  over exactly the images this epic converts.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A cryptographic module inventory exists for every KServe serving-stack image,\n58\t  listing each linked crypto library and its validation status.\n59\t- All KServe serving-stack images run correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift\n60\t  cluster using validated crypto modules, with no non-validated crypto in the\n61\t  request path, verified by test.\n62\t- The CI gating check covering KServe image builds fails a build that\n63\t  reintroduces non-validated crypto usage, verified by a test that intentionally\n64\t  reintroduces such usage and observes the gate fail.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-1 (P0) — KServe-image portion: images run on FIPS-enabled clusters with\n69\t  validated crypto, no non-validated crypto in the request path.\n70\t- HLR-3 (P1) — KServe-surface portion of the CI FIPS regression check\n71\t  (bundled: the check enforces over the same images this epic converts, so it\n72\t  is not separately schedulable).\n73\t\n74\t## Risks / Notes\n75\t\n76\t- The strategy does not enumerate which images link non-validated crypto; the\n77\t  scope audit resolves this and does not change the epic's shape.\n78\t- \"Serving data plane\" is interpreted as the KServe predictor data plane. If\n79\t  model-serving runtime images are also in scope, that work belongs to a\n80\t  separate strategy and epic set.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9638a8823e80ba9","agent_id":"a044fc504d2e0fe1d","session_id":"44bb4be5-e725-48c0-870c-d3c41c68193e","uuid":"abd5827b-25ab-4970-bbd7-8091b305fbca","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:12:02.334Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6dddcd0188c4d05","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":