67\tteam table, so this is properly recorded uncertainty, not a wrong assignment.\n68\t\n69\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n70\tNo Investigation epics — correctly justified under the Step 3 decision rule:\n71\tthe strategy states \"None on scope\" for open questions, and the one unresolved\n72\tdetail (which images link non-validated crypto) does not change which epics\n73\texist or what they do; it is audit work inside each conversion epic, gated by\n74\tthe inventory ACs. All four epics are Implementation and produce concrete\n75\tartifacts (inventories, converted images, CI gates, submitted evidence package,\n76\tpublished documentation). `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` are null everywhere,\n77\twhich is correct with no gates present.\n78\t\n79\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n80\tEvery epic carries the type-appropriate field (`ai_signals` for Implementation;\n81\t`investigation_signals` null as expected), and each has an ai-signals file whose\n82\trationales match the frontmatter values. Spot-checks hold up: E001's\n83\t`architecture_claims: 1` cites kserve.md corroborating the serving-stack\n84\tpremise; E002's `architecture_claims: 0` and `repo_access: 0` are honest scores\n85\tfor a component with no provisioned context file (the calibration-miss pattern\n86\trequires a covering context file, which does not exist for Platform Operator);\n87\tE003 carries the negative external_dependency and human_process_gates signals\n88\tthat the lab and review board warrant; E004's `human_process_gates: -1` matches\n89\tthe docs technical-review gate. E001's `human_process_gates: +1` is correctly\n90\tscoped — the review board gates the evidence submission (E003), not the code\n91\tconversion. No arithmetic checked (pipeline-computed).\n92\t\n93\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n94\tAll epics have testable ACs. The CI-gate ACs on E001/E002 are verified by an\n95\tintentional-reintroduction test — strongly testable. E004 carries the\n96\trule-mandated te