{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0f9d328cdf365ef","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 0\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: -1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 0\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 0\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAssembles the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model serving\n34\tstack — cryptographic module inventory, build attestations, and test results —\n35\tand submits it through the security review board to the external accredited\n36\tcertification laboratory.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Consolidate the cryptographic module inventory from the FIPS conversion\n41\t  audits of all serving-stack images in scope (KServe components and the\n42\t  Platform Operator).\n43\t- Collect the build attestations produced by the FIPS-converted serving-stack\n44\t  image builds.\n45\t- Collect the test results demonstrating correct operation on FIPS-enabled\n46\t  OpenShift clusters using validated crypto modules, with no non-validated\n47\t  crypto in the request path.\n48\t- Assemble the package in the form required by the security review board and\n49\t  the certification laboratory, drive it through the review-board milestones,\n50\t  and submit it to the laboratory.\n51\t- Track the submission through lab triage.\n52\t\n53\tThis epic runs in parallel with the image conversion work: the conversion\n54\toutputs (attestations, test results) are content the package includes, enforced\n55\tby the acceptance criteria below rather than by a scheduling dependency.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- The evidence package includes the cryptographic module inventory covering\n60\t  every serving-stack image in scope.\n61\t- The evidence package includes the build attestations produced by the\n62\t  FIPS-converted serving-stack image builds.\n63\t- The evidence package includes the test results demonstrating correct\n64\t  operation on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules with no\n65\t  non-validated crypto in the request path.\n66\t- The evidence package is assembled in the form required by the security\n67\t  review board and submitted through the security review board to the external\n68\t  certification laboratory.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-2 (P0) — full: compliance evidence package (module inventory, build\n73\t  attestations, test results) assembled and submitted through the security\n74\t  review board to the external certification lab.\n75\t\n76\t## Risks / Notes\n77\t\n78\t- Laboratory turnaround is historically six to nine months and security review\n79\t  board sign-off occurs at defined milestones; both are externally controlled\n80\t  and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. This epic's deliverable ends\n81\t  at submission through the security review board — the certification outcome\n82\t  and its timing are outside the strategy's control. The submission is expected\n83\t  to be triaged/acknowledged by the laboratory after intake, but lab triage is\n84\t  an external party's action and is therefore tracked as an expectation here\n85\t  rather than an acceptance criterion.\n86\t- The package spans the whole serving stack (KServe components and the\n87\t  Platform Operator); the KServe component is recorded as the primary Jira\n88\t  component for routing.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88e4a70625b8fdc2","agent_id":"a0d230977e6671217","session_id":"44bb4be5-e725-48c0-870c-d3c41c68193e","uuid":"5967e054-44e5-4c78-8289-3cc82c1df2de","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:16:20.628Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0f9d328cdf365ef","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013"}
